  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Cole gave them six scoreless frames and it still wasn't enough.",
    "what_this_means": "They had the game after four innings, leading by one through a pitching duel neither team could break open. Eight strikeouts across the lineup. Seven runners left on base, none of them converted, the offense locked behind an invisible door from the third inning onward. The Dodgers scored twice in the seventh. The game's only multi-run moment. And the Yankees never answered. One hit came too late. This is what happens when pitching holds tight enough to win and the bats decide not to show. The gap between a chance and a result kept widening. They wasted the margin Cole bought them.",
